  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 306 AM EDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThursday through Monday...\n\nFairly complex upper level pattern will be found across the CONUS at \nthe start of the period.  Hybrid Rex Block is forecast to be in \nprogress across the eastern US with a deep upper level low moving \nthrough the Mid-Atlantic while deepening.  This will result in an \nearly season east coast low that will move into New England over the \nweekend bring widespread rain and wind to those areas.\n\nFurther west across our area, the upper level trough axis will \ndepart to our east while a strong mid-level ridge over the Plains \nwill gradually build eastward toward the Ohio Valley.  The core of \nthe ridge will likely remain west of the Ohio Valley resulting in a \ncontinued northerly flow across our region.  The overall pattern \nwill keep the Thursday through Sunday period dry with below normal \ntemperatures continuing.\n\nFor Thursday, we should see a gradient of temperature across the \nregion with the coolest air residing across the Bluegrass region. \nHighs over there will top out in the lower 70s with mid-70s in the I-\n65 corridor and points west.  Under the northerly flow, temps will \nreally start to cool Thursday night and Friday morning with lows \ndropping into the upper 40s over SE Indiana and across much of the \nBluegrass.  Temps will likely dip to around 50 in the I-65 corridor \nwith lower 50s out back in the I-165 region.  Highs on Friday will \nagain feature a NE to SW gradient with highs in the Bluegrass in the \nlow-mid 70s with mid-upper 70s in the I-65 region back toward the I-\n165 corridor.  Lows Friday night and Saturday morning look to be \neven cooler with mid-upper 40s in the Bluegrass with low-mid 50s out \nwest of I-65.  If we can decouple and get clear skies, it is \npossible that some of our typical cooler spots could hit the upper \n30s/lower 40s Saturday morning.\n\nA beautiful fall weekend is in store for much of the region. Current \nblended guidance is likely too warm through this period.  Highs on \nSaturday/Sunday will be solidly in the 70s with overnight lows in \nthe mid-upper 40s in the northeast areas and lower 50s in the \nsouthwest.  Dry weather is expected to continue on Monday with a \nslight warming trend.  Most areas on Monday will again see temps \nsolidly in the 70s.",
